WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:08.820
hey everyone welcome to another
installments of Harry Potter theory in

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:13.380
this video we'll be discussing Severus
Snape, his ability to fly, and exploring the

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:18.630
question: was he a vampire? we don't see
or hear about vampires too much in the

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:22.109
Harry Potter story and the following
blurb from Pottermore gives us a brief

00:00:22.109 --> 00:00:26.160
introduction to the topic "although
vampires exist in the world of Harry

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.670
Potter as shown by the literature that
Harry and his friends study and defense

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:33.870
against the dark arts they play no
meaningful part in the story the vampire

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:37.800
myth is so rich and has been exploited
so many times in literature and on film

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.700
that I felt that there was little I
could add to the tradition in any case

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:45.809
vampires are a tradition of Eastern
Europe and in general I tried to draw

00:00:45.809 --> 00:00:49.410
from British mythology and folklore
when creating adversaries for Harry

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:53.910
aside from passing mentions therefore
the only vampire whom Harry meets in the

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:57.719
books is sanguine II in half-blood
Prince who makes a faintly comic

00:00:57.719 --> 00:01:02.010
appearance at a party" but I'm not
completely buying this here's why I

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:05.939
think that Severus Snape makes the
perfect vampire and why I think that his

00:01:05.939 --> 00:01:10.439
character possesses many of the defining
characteristics of the vampire, a vampire

00:01:10.439 --> 00:01:14.520
is defined as a creature from folklore
that is subsists by feeding on the vital

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:18.720
essence generally in the form of blood
of the living but there's more to a

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.560
vampire than drinking blood in order to
survive let's look at some of the

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.640
defining characteristics of a vampire
and how they relate to Snape the first

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.240
major characteristic of a vampire that I
want to touch on is avoiding sunlight

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.070
it's well known that vampires, like some
animals, avoid light, they have a tendency

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:38.460
to inhabit dark conditions and some
spend their lives in permanent darkness

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:42.750
this describes Snape quite well.
Snape's office in the dungeons of

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:47.040
Hogwarts is described as follows: "the
office was a gloomy and dimly lit room

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:51.600
found in the school dungeons, the shadowy
walls were lined with shelves of large

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.100
glass jars filled with slimy revolting
things such as bits of animals and

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.979
plants floating in potions of varying
colors"

00:01:58.979 --> 00:02:02.909
Snape's office is perhaps the darkest
and eeriest of all of the offices

00:02:02.909 --> 00:02:07.710
belonging to Hogwarts staff and the
dimly lit gloomy room in the dungeons of

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:10.860
the school seems like the perfect place
for one type of creature:

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:16.110
a vampire, and yes we have seen Severus
Snape in direct sunlight on occasion but

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:19.890
he might have figured out a way to spend
time in sunlight as we know that he is

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:23.820
an incredibly talented wizard and
excellent potioneer. Next up we have

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:27.840
heightened senses vampires are said to
have heightened vision hearing and sense

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.860
of smell, though I don't have too many
specific examples of Snape exhibiting

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:36.090
super heightened senses he does seem to
have a bit of a habit of making an

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:39.330
appearance whenever students are
breaking rules -wandering out of their

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:42.450
common rooms when they shouldn't be or
meddling in matters that do not relate

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:46.680
to them. Sure he's always lurking around
the castle at night but he also seems to

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:50.040
be particularly aware of what's
happening at the castle at all times. If

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:53.940
you can recall the night that Harry
wandered into the restricted section of

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.209
the library with his invisibility cloak,
you'll remember that he bumped into

00:02:57.209 --> 00:03:01.080
Snape and Quirrell. Even though Harry was
under the invisibility cloak, an

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:05.160
extremely advanced magical artifact, 
Snape still had a strong intuition that

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:09.180
someone was there, this was shown by him
reaching into the air. I think that this

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:13.140
is a reflection of his perhaps
heightened senses. Next up we have

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:17.280
morphing, or in the Harry Potter world-
transfiguration, vampires are said to

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:21.930
have the ability to morph into another
form like a bat often behind the Shroud

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:26.280
of a cloak. After morphing they disappear
creating the illusion that they have

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:30.390
vanished flying away from their
aggressor on one occasion Snape does

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:34.470
exactly this. In the Deathly Hallows we
see Snape jump from the tower of the

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:38.370
Hogwarts castle the following passage
depicts Snape flying in front of

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:42.480
McGonagall, Harry, and some of the
students "he jumped" said Professor

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:47.760
McGonagall "you mean he's dead" Harry
sprinted to the window "no he's not dead"

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:52.380
said McGonagall. What this passage
suggests is that Snape flew away JK

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:55.799
Rowling is reported to have stated that
all Wizards have the power of flight

00:03:55.799 --> 00:04:00.660
innately but the vast vast majority need
a broom to achieve it in Voldemort case

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:04.230
he was so focused and powerful that he
was able to channel the power to fly

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:08.070
unsupported harnessing the energy
through himself rather than through a

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:10.890
broom
maybe Snape did the same but I really

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:14.820
think that he achieved it in another way
going back to the first passage where

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:17.910
Snape jumps from the Hogwarts Tower
there's one line that really piqued my

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:22.380
interest I think that it could shed some
light on his method of flying. Harry saw

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:27.030
a huge
bat-like shape flying through the darkness. As far

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:30.980
as the books are concerned, when Voldemort
uses unsupported flight he maintains his

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:33.980
original form, So what's this bat like
shape?

00:04:33.990 --> 00:04:38.550
Why would Snape resemble a bat? My
answer: Snape's a vampire. If you

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:41.520
aren't sold on that theory
then another explanation for the bat

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:46.500
like shape could be that he was A. an
animagus or B. used transfiguration to

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.370
turn his arms into wings Snape was a
gifted wizard and he was once the

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:54.599
student of Horace Slughorn who was known
to be talented at Transfiguration. This

00:04:54.599 --> 00:04:58.710
would not have been out of the question
for him to achieve and last of all just

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:03.960
look at Snape, now let's compare him to a
couple of vampires. Not sold yet?

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:09.419
Fair enough this is just an idea. What do
you guys think? Was Snape a vampire, an

00:05:09.419 --> 00:05:13.860
unregistered animagus, a talented
practitioner of transfiguration, or an

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:18.599
expert at unsupported flight? Let me know
down in the comment section below. Until

00:05:18.599 --> 00:05:28.490
next time, you're a wizard Harry.

